Notes						
•	All seven sites are past construction complete and are held out of service pending utility-owned equipment installation and SCADA integration. TCS-02 §5 prohibits Permission to Operate absent live telemetry for sites ≥500 kW.					
•	Utility equipment supply status is tracked in the SCADA/EMS Supplier Lead-Time Report (Marcus Deele, 06/30/2025): two complete RTU + POI recloser sets are scheduled to arrive 08/2025; the next confirmed delivery is 03/2026. Current approved suppliers are Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc. (RTU) and Norstead Power Controls, LLC (POI recloser), both quoting ~8-month lead times.					
•	"Requested Priority" entries against the two Brookfen USD school arrays were added to this register on 07/02/2025 following written escalation from Rosa Camarena, Facilities Director, Brookfen Unified School District. No other sites have priority claims on file as of this revision.					
•	The Alleron Community Solar Initiative — Rowan Hill row carries a contracted grant-funding in-service date of 09/30/2025, recorded in this register at application intake.					
•	Deployment sequencing of scarce utility equipment is governed by OG-17 (Equipment Deployment Prioritization Guideline, effective 04/07/2025). This register is an inputs roster; it does not itself assign sequencing.					
•	Register is maintained by the DER Program Office and refreshed on the weekly queue export cycle. Additions and removals are logged against the revision block above.					
Prepared by: DER Program Office, Alleniom Utilities — 07/14/2025.						
[Sheet: Column Definitions]
Column Definitions	
Register: Completed Sites Awaiting Utility Equipment  ·  Doc DER-EQP-COMPL Rev 3  ·  07/14/2025	
Column	Definition
Site Name	Site identifier as recorded in the DER Program queue.
Site Type	Customer category (municipal essential service, grant-funded community solar, school district, commercial C&I).
Contracted In-Service or Grant Deadline	Written contracted in-service date or grant-funding milestone, where one exists on file. Blank where no such deadline has been contracted or funded.
Queue Date	Date the interconnection application received a queue position under the DER Program.
Construction Complete Date	Date the site's customer-side construction was reported complete by the applicant and confirmed by field inspection. Not the same as PTO.
Required Devices	Utility-owned equipment outstanding: RTU (per TCS-02 §5) and/or POI recloser (per DPS-07 §4.2 / per applicable Form ER-11 determination).
Requested Priority	Priority level asserted by the customer or requesting stakeholder in written correspondence. Recorded as received; not a program determination.